{"schema":"learning-v2-theory.v1","lesson":9,"lang":"pl","title":"Co się dzieje teraz","sections":[{"num":"01","title":"Czego się nauczysz","defaultOpen":true,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"W lekcji 6 mówiłeś o tym, co dzieje się regularnie: I work, she cooks. Teraz — o tym, co dzieje się właśnie teraz, na twoich oczach: «obserwuję ptaki», «lód się topi», «ona nie próbuje dżemu», «czy zamek działa?»."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I am observing the birds.","translation":"Obserwuję ptaki.","hi":"am observing"},{"en":"The ice is melting.","translation":"Lód się topi.","hi":"is melting"},{"en":"She is not tasting the jam.","translation":"Ona nie próbuje dżemu.","hi":"is not tasting"},{"en":"Is the zipper working?","translation":"Czy zamek działa?","hi":"Is"}]}]},{"num":"02","title":"am / is / are + czynność z -ing","defaultOpen":true,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Po polsku «obserwuję» to i «teraz», i «zwykle». Po angielsku to, co dzieje się teraz, mówi się inaczej: am, is lub are i czynność z końcówką -ing. I am observing — «właśnie obserwuję». Potrzebne są obie części."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"kto","accent":true},{"text":"am / is / are","accent":true},{"text":"czynność + ing","accent":false}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I am observing the birds.","translation":"Obserwuję ptaki.","hi":"am observing"},{"en":"She is watching a caterpillar.","translation":"Ona przygląda się gąsienicy.","hi":"is watching"},{"en":"They are using a magnifier.","translation":"Używają lupy.","hi":"are using"},{"en":"I am knocking at the door.","translation":"Pukam do drzwi.","hi":"am knocking"},{"en":"A visitor is waiting.","translation":"Gość czeka.","hi":"is waiting"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"I observing the birds.","right":"I am observing the birds."},{"wrong":"Am observing the birds.","right":"I am observing the birds."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"She","after":"watching a caterpillar.","options":["is","are","—"],"answer":"is","why":"Przed czynnością z -ing potrzebne jest is; z she — is."}}]},{"num":"03","title":"am, is, are — jak w lekcji 1","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Które słowo wziąć, decyduje «kto», jak na samym początku kursu. I — am, he, she, it i jedna rzecz — is, you, we, they — are: I am sighing, the ice is melting, we are marching."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I am sighing with relief.","translation":"Wzdycham z ulgą.","hi":"am"},{"en":"He is sneezing.","translation":"On kicha.","hi":"is"},{"en":"The firefly is glowing now.","translation":"Świetlik teraz świeci.","hi":"is"},{"en":"We are marching.","translation":"Maszerujemy.","hi":"are"},{"en":"The leaves are whirling.","translation":"Liście wirują.","hi":"are"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"The leaves is whirling.","right":"The leaves are whirling."},{"wrong":"We is marching.","right":"We are marching."}]}]},{"num":"04","title":"Jak się pisze -ing","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Zwykle po prostu dodaje się -ing: watch → watching. Jeśli słowo kończy się na nieme e, e znika: make → making. Jeśli na krótką samogłoskę i jedną spółgłoskę, spółgłoska się podwaja: sit → sitting, hop → hopping."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I am making my portfolio.","translation":"Składam swoje portfolio.","hi":"making"},{"en":"I am sitting.","translation":"Siedzę.","hi":"sitting"},{"en":"I am submitting my work.","translation":"Oddaję swoją pracę.","hi":"submitting"},{"en":"The sparrow is hopping.","translation":"Wróbel skacze.","hi":"hopping"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"I am makeing my portfolio.","right":"I am making my portfolio."},{"wrong":"I am siting.","right":"I am sitting."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"I am","after":".","options":["siting","sitting","sit"],"answer":"sitting","why":"W sit jest krótka samogłoska i jedna spółgłoska, więc t się podwaja."}}]},{"num":"05","title":"«Nie» — not po am, is, are","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Po polsku «nie» stoi przed czasownikiem: «nie zgaduję». Po angielsku not idzie zaraz po am, is, are: I am not guessing, she is not tasting the jam. Czynność z -ing zostaje."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"kto","accent":true},{"text":"am / is / are","accent":true},{"text":"not","accent":true},{"text":"czynność + ing","accent":false}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I am not guessing.","translation":"Nie zgaduję.","hi":"not"},{"en":"She is not tasting the jam.","translation":"Ona nie próbuje dżemu.","hi":"not"},{"en":"They are not looking.","translation":"Nie patrzą.","hi":"not"},{"en":"The wax is not melting.","translation":"Wosk się nie topi.","hi":"not"},{"en":"The drummer is not marching.","translation":"Perkusista nie maszeruje.","hi":"not"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"I not guessing.","right":"I am not guessing."},{"wrong":"She doesn't tasting the jam.","right":"She is not tasting the jam."},{"wrong":"They are not look.","right":"They are not looking."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"spot_slip","kind":"spot_slip","chips":["She","doesn't","tasting","the","jam"],"answerIndex":1,"hint":"Jedno słowo tu nie pasuje. Dotknij go.","fix":"Z -ing «nie» to is not: She is not tasting the jam."}}]},{"num":"06","title":"Pytanie: am, is, are na początek","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Pytanie buduje się jak w lekcji 2: am, is lub are idzie na początek. Is the ice melting? Are you inspecting the seam? Do i does nie są tu potrzebne — one są do pytań o nawyki."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"Am / Is / Are","accent":true},{"text":"kto","accent":true},{"text":"czynność + ing","accent":false},{"text":"?","accent":true}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"Are you inspecting the seam?","translation":"Sprawdzasz szew?","hi":"Are"},{"en":"Is she inspecting the lining?","translation":"Czy ona sprawdza podszewkę?","hi":"Is"},{"en":"Is the zipper working?","translation":"Czy zamek działa?","hi":"Is"},{"en":"Is he sighing?","translation":"Czy on wzdycha?","hi":"Is"},{"en":"Is the chocolate melting?","translation":"Czy czekolada się topi?","hi":"Is"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"You are inspecting the seam?","right":"Are you inspecting the seam?"},{"wrong":"Do you inspecting the seam?","right":"Are you inspecting the seam?"}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"word_bank","kind":"word_bank","prompt":"Zapytaj: «Czy czekolada się topi?»","answer":["Is","the","chocolate","melting"],"distractors":["Does","melt"]}}]},{"num":"07","title":"Teraz — czy zwykle?","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"I wear a sweatshirt — «noszę bluzę» (zwykle). I am sweating — «pocę się» (teraz). Po polsku to ta sama forma, a po angielsku różne zdania. Zadaj sobie pytanie: to nawyk czy właśnie teraz?"},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I wear a sweatshirt.","translation":"Noszę bluzę. *(zwykle)*","hi":"wear"},{"en":"I am sweating.","translation":"Pocę się. *(teraz)*","hi":"am sweating"},{"en":"The firefly is glowing now.","translation":"Świetlik teraz świeci.","hi":"is glowing"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"I sweat now.","right":"I am sweating."},{"wrong":"I am usually wearing a sweatshirt.","right":"I usually wear a sweatshirt."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"binary","kind":"binary","question":"Właśnie teraz lód na schodach się topi. Jak powiesz?","optionA":"The ice melts.","optionB":"The ice is melting.","correct":"B","explain":"To dzieje się teraz, więc is melting."}}]},{"num":"08","title":"Coś się dzieje — i gdzie","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Do zdania o tym, co się dzieje, łatwo dodać, gdzie: She is in the doorway. I am near the carousel. To znane is z miejscem — bez -ing, bo czynności tu nie ma."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"She is in the doorway.","translation":"Stoi w drzwiach.","hi":"is"},{"en":"I am near the carousel.","translation":"Jestem przy karuzeli.","hi":"am"},{"en":"She is murmuring to the baby.","translation":"Szepcze coś do dziecka.","hi":"is murmuring"},{"en":"My hands are trembling.","translation":"Drżą mi ręce.","hi":"are trembling"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"I am being near the carousel.","right":"I am near the carousel."}]}]},{"num":"09","title":"Błędy, które robi prawie każdy","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"I observing the birds.","right":"I am observing the birds."},{"wrong":"The leaves is whirling.","right":"The leaves are whirling."},{"wrong":"I am siting.","right":"I am sitting."},{"wrong":"I not guessing.","right":"I am not guessing."},{"wrong":"You are inspecting the seam?","right":"Are you inspecting the seam?"},{"wrong":"She doesn't tasting the jam.","right":"She is not tasting the jam."}]},{"kind":"tip","text":"Dwie części zawsze razem: am / is / are i -ing. Jest jedna — szukaj drugiej. Teraz — -ing, zwykle — jak w lekcji 6."}]},{"num":"10","title":"Co zabrać do ćwiczeń","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Teraz — am / is / are + czynność z -ing. «Nie» — not po am, is, are. Pytanie — am, is, are na początek. Pisz uważnie: making, sitting, hopping. Nawyk — jak w lekcji 6, bez -ing."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"They are using a magnifier.","translation":"Używają lupy.","hi":"are using"},{"en":"They are not looking.","translation":"Nie patrzą.","hi":"not"},{"en":"Is she inspecting the lining?","translation":"Czy ona sprawdza podszewkę?","hi":"Is"},{"en":"I am submitting my work.","translation":"Oddaję swoją pracę.","hi":"submitting"}]}]}],"sessionSection":{"1":"02","2":"02","3":"02","4":"02","5":"02","6":"02","7":"02","8":"02","9":"05","10":"05","11":"05","12":"05","13":"05","14":"05","15":"05","16":"05","17":"06","18":"06","19":"06","20":"06","21":"06","22":"06","23":"06","24":"06","25":"07","26":"07","27":"07","28":"07","29":"07","30":"07","31":"07","32":"07","33":"04","34":"04","35":"04","36":"04","37":"04","38":"04","39":"04","40":"04","41":"08","42":"08","43":"08","44":"08","45":"08","46":"08","47":"08","48":"08","49":"08","50":"08","51":"08","52":"08","53":"08","54":"08","55":"08","56":"08"}}
